  lfs-outline <batch_id> Generate + contract-repair LFS outlines
    Options:
      -w, --workers      Parallel Claude calls (default: 4)
      --model MODEL      Claude model (default: LFS_OUTLINE_MODEL or claude-sonnet-4-6)
      --force            Replace existing outlines
      --dry-run          Validate prompt mappings without API calls
      --max-attempts N   Generation + deterministic repair attempts (default: 3)
    Source-swipe prompts may include:
      ## SOURCE SWIPE
      scanner/tyver/.../copies/source-copy.md

  lfs-chief <batch_id>   Copy-chief generated LFS scripts into output-chiefed/
    Options:
      --input-subdir DIR   Raw script directory (default: output)
      --output-subdir DIR  Chiefed script directory (default: output-chiefed)
      --docs PATH          Chiefing doc file or directory; repeatable
      -w, --workers        Parallel Claude calls (default: 4)
      --dry-run            Run without writing output-chiefed/

  lfs-semantic <batch_id> Check whether scripts follow saved outlines
    Options:
      --output-subdir DIR  Script directory to check/repair (default: output-chiefed)
      -w, --workers        Parallel Claude calls (default: 4)
      --max-attempts N     Repair attempts after failed judge pass (default: 2)
      --dry-run            Judge without writing repairs

  rank-combos <target>   Rank modular component combinations worst→best (Inceptly)
    Arguments:
      target               Product code (NRJNT, NOOR) or batch ID with modular/
    Options:
      --axes A,B           Two axes to rank (default: hooks,bridges)
                           Options: hooks, bridges, cores, ctas
      --hooks/--bridges/   Override specific component file path
        --cores/--ctas
      --output PATH        Output file (default: <modular>/rank-report_AxB.json)
      --model MODEL        Claude model (default: claude-opus-4-5)
      --json               Output raw JSON to stdout
